yxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T18:59:08-08:00","id":783192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/783060-exactly-how-easy-hard-possible-is-it-to-kill-a-true-fae?p=783183#post783183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> White Wolf, please confirm. Is 4chan a True Fae?</div> </div> </div> </div>How about we go stab it with cold iron first, then ask questions later?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T19:26:13-08:00","id":783201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/783060-exactly-how-easy-hard-possible-is-it-to-kill-a-true-fae?p=783192#post783192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about we go stab it with cold iron first, then ask questions later?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would answer both of my questions!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T20:39:09-08:00","id":783218,"title":"","content":"If you've got a blade made from cold iron and can lure them into the mortal world, that puts the odds in your favor. Anything else will be one hell of a fight on your hands. If you actually try to fight them in their own realm, that's what we call &quot;natural selection&quot; at work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T10:27:42-08:00","id":784838,"title":"","content":"Following the guidelines in Equinox Road, almost every Fae has 1-5 additional manifestations. They can be killed individually, but doing so tends to be immensely difficult and dangerous. Granted, Autumn Nightmares has a selection of True Fae that can likely be beaten by a moderately experienced motley, so how tough it is really depends on what source you're using.<br /> <br /> For the most common and interactive form that mortals are likely to encounter in the mortal world, the Actor form, they're just especially powerful monsters and can theoretically be killed in combat. Killing an actor seriously hurts the True Fae it belongs to, but will not kill the Fae itself unless all its other manifestations have been destroyed as well. There are example characters, including Grandfather Thunder, who are known or at least rumored to have killed a Keeper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T00:13:06-08:00","id":785231,"title":"","content":"To kill a True Fae, you must find a way to take away his name ( not Entitlement, but Name) since it's the only thing which defines them, lacking a real soul . No idea how.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T11:28:56-08:00","id":794288,"title":"","content":"The True Fae are composed of a Name and a variable number of Titles. Titles can be spun into various forms: Actors, Props, Wisps and Realms. Actors are the ones that look like people and have normal stats. High, but normal. You can kill an Actor the same way you'd kill anything else. Props are objects; they can do one thing perfectly and irresistibly, and can only be destroyed by one particular means. Expose them to that one individual weakness, they just... cease. Wisps are basically mobs. They can be killed like any mob. Realms are buildings and landscapes. Killing them is very tricky. Finally, if you destroy all the Fae's Titles, you can kill the Name, which always manifests as an Actor. Fae can steal Titles from one another, but I don't think changelings can do that. You can face a fae's Name, even fight it, while it still have Titles available, but you *cannot* kill it or even hurt it without destroying the Titles first. So if one of the Gentry takes the form of an Arabian Nights king, the king could be its Name, the palace a Realm, the slave girls a pack of Wisps, his crown a Prop, and his wazir an Actor. Even if you managed to kill the wazir and the slaves and topple the palace, you'd still have to find the crown's sole weakness before you could harm the king. Perhaps you need to immerse it in liquid darkness, or expose it to the light of the moon at midday (both of these are quite possible: matte black paint would qualify as liquid darkness and the moon shines at midday during fall and winter). That's important: a prop's weakness is always discoverable and always possible, and often fairly simple once learned. No &quot;place it between the sea and the strand&quot; sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 12-28-2015, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T12:01:56-08:00","id":794306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/783060-exactly-how-easy-hard-possible-is-it-to-kill-a-true-fae?p=794288#post794288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can face a fae's Name, even fight it, while it still have Titles available, but you *cannot* kill it or even hurt it without destroying the Titles first.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Name doesn't even manifest until all the Titles are gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T14:01:02-08:00","id":794374,"title":"","content":"I don't recall Equinox Road specifying that. One way or another, you absolutely must eliminate the Titles before you actually engage the Name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T14:31:45-08:00","id":794389,"title":"","content":"Satchel's right. The Name doesn't manifest until the Titles are eliminated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T18:40:38-08:00","id":794530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/783060-exactly-how-easy-hard-possible-is-it-to-kill-a-true-fae?p=783183#post783183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> White Wolf, please confirm. Is 4chan a True Fae?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. We like to maintain a modicum of optimism in our game lines, to give you some contrast to the darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T20:00:41-08:00","id":794566,"title":"","content":"Whenever I heard about hunting on the True Fae....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ry7PcYtKPhA?t=16s\" data-code=\"Ry7PcYtKPhA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Ry7PcYtKPhA/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I needed to share that in this topic after watching <b>Nightmare Before Christmas</b> few days ago - it such fitting... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-28-2015, 11:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T04:43:47-08:00","id":794758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/783060-exactly-how-easy-hard-possible-is-it-to-kill-a-true-fae?p=785231#post785231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To kill a True Fae, you must find a way to take away his name ( not Entitlement, but Name) since it's the only thing which defines them, lacking a real soul . No idea how.</div> </div> </div> </div> Equinox Road says that a comparatively quick way to end one of the Gentry is to make it swear a Pledge on its True Name, and then fool them into breaking that Pledge. Some say that Gentry who fall for this suffer a spectacular destruction that sweeps across their every Title, while others say they simply vanish like a popped soap bubble. <br /> <br /> Good luck pulling that off on a &quot;species&quot; of superlative liars and cheaters, though.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I strongly disagree with making Anonymous a True Fae. There's something deeply human about them, you know? They're just people who let their true colors show because they have no face. It's like a masquerade or carnival in a new medium: the idea itself is very old. In fact, considering the creativity of some of the stunts and shenanigans they do, I'd say actual Gentry could be outsmarted by them. No changelings or fae-touched, just some dudes who were pissed off at the weirdo who's been slaughtering cats in their city. <br /> <br /> I feel that saying the efforts both fair and foul of people like these were supernatural makes them less fascinating. I mean, just read this <b><a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/U7scF.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this parody of V's speech from V For Vendetta </a></b>. Gloriously stupid and stupidly glorious? Sounds like humanity to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-29-2015, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T09:01:41-08:00","id":794874,"title":"","content":"I'd say that if the Gentry are living stories, they need to be killed in a way that makes a satisfying <i>conclusion </i>to their story. The more appropriate and mythical the death, the greater the chance that they'll stay dead. It helps if you've been personally wronged by the Fae you're trying to kill, and if you've sworn mighty oaths against it or otherwise dedicated yourself to its destruction. It helps a lot if you can somehow turn its own power against it, or otherwise arrange an ironic fate. A Fae warlord's former champion slaying it in single combat with the sword it gave her would probably work. A complete stranger sniping the same Fae from cover with a cold iron bullet probably <i>wouldn't</i> work, at least not permanently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T11:45:12-08:00","id":794989,"title":"","content":"As cool as I think the breakdown of Fae into True Name and the various types of Titles is, I kind of like DSPaul's take. At the very least, I'd consider that sort of thing as an effective way to kill a Title at the very least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T17:55:35-08:00","id":795248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/783060-exactly-how-easy-hard-possible-is-it-to-kill-a-true-fae?p=794989#post794989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As cool as I think the breakdown of Fae into True Name and the various types of Titles is, I kind of like DSPaul's take. At the very least, I'd consider that sort of thing as an effective way to kill a Title at the very least.</div> </div> </div> </div>It pretty much <i>only</i> works for Titles, seeing as that's how Legend combat plays out beyond the abstracted rules in Game of Immortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T15:44:10-08:00","id":797051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/783060-exactly-how-easy-hard-possible-is-it-to-kill-a-true-fae?p=795248#post795248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It pretty much <i>only</i> works for Titles, seeing as that's how Legend combat plays out beyond the abstracted rules in Game of Immortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna be honest, if I was the story-teller, I wouldn't care what the rules said on that one. If I had a group of players sit and ponder the nature of the fae to that extent, come up with that idea, execute it, and actually pull it off, I'd give it to them, names and titles be damned. Because that was brilliant.<br /> <br /> Maybe call it a house-rule or something. Every Fae has a bane in the form of an event or situation which acts as a dramatically satisfying conclusion to the story they embody. Who determines what's dramatically satisfying? I do. I'm the story-teller damn it.<br /> <br /> You could make that really interesting. Like now motleys have a real shot at taking down their old keepers if they can just find this one bit of information and determine what old story or fairy tale their keepers embodied. So that gives them a really strong motivation to go back into the hedge and poke around, looking for clues, having adventures, seeing weird shit. If you're worried about that making the fae too weak or easily defeatable, you could add that since they are stories, and stories exist in the mind, they grow exponentially more powerful when somebody else knows their story, because it gives them more of themselves or something like that. That balances the temptation to search for the story with the knowledge that doing so will make your adversary way harder to actually best, even with knowledge of his weakness. And it also explains why maybe some people around the hedge and arcadia and stuff would know or have clues to that story, because if the fae feels that they can be trusted or (much more likely) controlled, then giving them that information, or even snippets of it, would greatly increase their power. <br /> <br /> If you don't like that, maybe rule that since the fae are stories, then they are intrinsically aware of anyone who knows their stories and where they are. Or, if you want to be really mean, it gives them some kind of power over you and your will. After all, stories exist in the mind. If you know the fae's story, and the fae IS his story, then logically speaking, the fae is now inside your mind. Or as logically as anything concerning the fae can be","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T15:56:40-08:00","id":797056,"title":"","content":"Heave you ever read Equinox Road?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T15:58:25-08:00","id":797057,"title":"","content":"Haven't had the pleasure I'm afraid. I probably have access to it, since the Mrs. owns basically every CoD book there is.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Sure enough, here it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T16:34:50-08:00","id":797074,"title":"","content":"Okay. Rather than get it bit bit and second hand, may I recommend reading Chapter 3, as well as the Appendix? because I find there's less discrepancy here than seems to be seen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T20:50:39-08:00","id":797172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/783060-exactly-how-easy-hard-possible-is-it-to-kill-a-true-fae?p=797051#post797051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna be honest, if I was the story-teller, I wouldn't care what the rules said on that one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Irrelevant to the quotation, seeing as the only reference I made to the rules was to say that the Fae taking Titles from one another is only represented in the rules in the abstracted terms of a minigame that can frame arcs of a chronicle.<br /> <br /> The Fae aren't <i>specific</i> stories save in the sense that a specific Fae is the story of itself. They're a set of patterns in events manifested as a number of phenomena proportionate to their metaphysical fortunes. &quot;Prince Wadjet&quot; is the Name taken by the force of destiny that drives and empowers the River of Sorrows, the Scroll of Golden Reeds, and the King Cloaked in Dust, all of which serve to fulfill Wadjet's designs in Faerie and beyond, but &quot;bringing a satisfying end to the story of Wadjet&quot; without cutting the Prince off from all of his assets amounts to ensuring he wins Transcendence and hoping this doesn't have any particularly terrible consequences for the wider world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T16:55:03-08:00","id":798024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/783060-exactly-how-easy-hard-possible-is-it-to-kill-a-true-fae?p=783067#post783067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More Details in Autumn Nightmares, Equinox Road, and the upcoming Second Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div> Is Autumn Nightmares/Equinox Road and and Second Edition True Fae simular in any way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T17:05:02-08:00","id":798026,"title":"","content":"The True Fae you have always known are still here-just sharper, more refined, much more condensed.<br /> <br /> And terrifying again. Very terrifying.<br /> <br /> More will have to wait until Dave spoils.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T08:49:49-08:00","id":803776,"title":"","content":"Oh my god. I just read the Changeling crossover section in the Demon Storytellers Guide. Spoilers, perhaps unsanctioned, follow.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So it looks like Huntsmen are in Lost 2E what Wisps were in Lost 1E- servants that are extensions of the True Fae, and maybe even parts of a Title? Also, here's a potential gauge of how mind-numbingly powerful the Gentry are in Arcadia. One of the Banished? Those True Fae that were at Wyrd 5 or less? A <i>severely diminished </i>True Fae, who fled Arcadia fearing utter destruction, is according to this part of the Demon Storytellers Guide, of Wyrd 8 or higher, with 20 dots of Contracts, and superhuman Attributes and Skills. This is an Old God in exile- fearing for its existence. What on earth are the fully powered Gentry like if this counts as severely diminished for them?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T10:14:52-08:00","id":803822,"title":"","content":"That same section says that a Banished Fae is only as powerful as a high powered Changeling, and weaker than their counterparts. I'm not entirely clear whether it's saying that high powered Changelings should be Wyrd 8+ and have 20 dots of contracts, or if that's the baseline for a Fae choosing to manifest in the mortal realm, and the Banished are weaker than that, more on the 10 dots of contracts high power Changeling level from the previous section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T11:33:36-08:00","id":803876,"title":"","content":"I only skimmed the section in an initial glance through, and didn't see the particulars, but yeah, you've only seen the tip of the iceberg if that's what it gave.<br /> <br /> As for Huntsmen? No, they aren't like Wisps. More like........[REDACTED].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T11:41:40-08:00","id":803886,"title":"","content":"I think it's pretty heavily implied that Hunstmen are made of whatever a Changeling left behind in Arcadia. Probably upon acquiring their Seeming, which is where all the &quot;btw there are bodyparts of you in Arcadia&quot; info comes from.<br /> <br /> I bet the name of the resource Huntsmen get probably indicates that Huntsmen are way more than just people who drag you back to the True Fae. I bet you they've got their own personalities and yearn for either the changeling himself or something the changeling has, and could either be bargained with (as per the original Huntsman) or they just have &quot;creepy stalker&quot; imagery associated with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T11:49:20-08:00","id":803893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/783060-exactly-how-easy-hard-possible-is-it-to-kill-a-true-fae?p=803886#post803886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's pretty heavily implied that Hunstmen are made of whatever a Changeling left behind in Arcadia. Probably upon acquiring their Seeming, which is where all the &quot;btw there are bodyparts of you in Arcadia&quot; info comes from.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's some of that, but nowhere near the whole of the Huntsmen.<br /> <br /> God, I wish I could just tell y'all the one word I use to describe them. But alas, 'till time and tide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T03:52:17-08:00","id":804329,"title":"","content":"The fact Huntsmen can ignore the things granted by Courts that protect changelings from Gentry shows they're pretty distinct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T12:04:54-08:00","id":804599,"title":"","content":"(Applies sledgehammer to NDAs in hopes of loosening them.)<br /> <br /> I'm eager to learn about the Huntsmen, myself. Writing up a villain with a fox motif and a band of nine &quot;Tails&quot; who act as her muscle on Earth.<br /> <br /> &quot;Don't lower your guard.<br /> Helvetica's assassins<br /> are after your book.&quot;<br /> <br /> -Ziggy Zapf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T16:45:34-08:00","id":805597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/783060-exactly-how-easy-hard-possible-is-it-to-kill-a-true-fae?p=804599#post804599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Applies sledgehammer to NDAs in hopes of loosening them.)<br /> <br /> I'm eager to learn about the Huntsmen, myself. Writing up a villain with a fox motif and a band of nine &quot;Tails&quot; who act as her muscle on Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm suddenly reminded of a rather chilling story seed from one of the Orpheus books. Members of a particular class Specter (twisted, inhuman ghosts consumed by their darker emotions) were called &quot;Kindly Angels,&quot; and could appear to children in any number of benign forms in order to lure them into injury, suffering, and eventually death. The book gave as an example one which presented itself as the title character of <i>The Fantastic Mr. Fox</i>, having first manifested to an elementary school class who were reading the book (this was well before the more recent film adaptation).<br /> <br /> I might just have to steal the idea for a Huntsmen who delights on preying on Changelings with families. Even if the Lost aren't normally able to bear or sire children, there are probably more than a few who already had children when they were Taken, or who have young siblings, nieces, or nephews.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, For those who don't know, Orpheus was a limited game line (much like Changeling 1e) introduced toward the end of the original run of the Classic WoD. In it, the PCs are sort of like Ghostbusters, if the Ghostbusters used astral projection and freaky ghost powers instead of proton packs, and were big-time corporate sellouts. It was extremely awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 01-10-2016, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}